{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions","id":844555,"title":"Got W20. any advices and couple o' questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-09T09:23:29-08:00","id":844555,"title":"Got W20. any advices and couple o' questions","content":"i recently got W20 and i gotta say, i loved the book.<br /> i used to play years ago with my original group/pack back in highschool and the book bought a lot of memories back.<br /> <br /> i been dming Mage for a long time now, love HtR and DtF. But dunno why, i find it a bit tricky to get a gasp on the mythos of Werewolf. i think its a huge game and universe but its hard for me to come up with ideas for games. to give it the epic/tragic style.. any advices on adventures, books or stories i should read from the Werewolf the apocalypse mythos?<br /> <br /> also, in the W20 book. is there any art on Zhyzhak? im trying to find the She-Wolf of the Wyrm but i can seem to find her","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:40:13-08:00","id":844635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions#post844555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been dming Mage for a long time now, love HtR and DtF. But dunno why, i find it a bit tricky to get a gasp on the mythos of Werewolf. i think its a huge game and universe but its hard for me to come up with ideas for games. to give it the epic/tragic style.. any advices on adventures, books or stories i should read from the Werewolf the apocalypse mythos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Settingwise there's three books I highly recommend picking up. First on my list is <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/124116/W20-Rage-Across-the-World?cPath=1_19942\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Rage Across the World</a> which is pretty much the companion book to W20, adding not just new systems, gifts, rites and totems but setting material on what its like in Septs and caerns as well as locations around the world. Frankly I consider it a must have for any group running W20. <br /> <br /> Next is <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/139920/W20-Umbra-The-Velvet-Shadow?src=slider_view\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Umbra: the Velvet Shadow</a>. As the name implies, its all about the Umbra and its denizens which give the nature of the Garou means that any pack is going experience quite a bit of.<br /> <br /> Finally <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138407/W20-Book-of-the-Wyrm?src=slider_view\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Book of the Wyrm</a> because epic heroes need epic foes. It's every you don't want to know about the Wyrm and all its foul minions but need to know.<br /> <br /> There are other books I could recommend but those three will give you a good spread of info on the world Garou live in, the Umbra and spirts they regularly interact with and the foes they battle.<br /> <br /> For adventures, I suggest looking at <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/251/Rite-of-Passage?cPath=1_6538&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Rite of Passage</a>. While it is an old First Edition and does need bit of fine-tuning and modernizing, it does serve as a great starting point. In it, the PCs are relatively new Garou going through their Rite of Passage to become Garou proper.<br /> <br /> If, and only if, you're willing you're willing to do some conversion work, the adventure in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2360/Werewolf-The-Forsaken-Demo-Full?cPath=1_184&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Quickstart</a> could also work well for a starting point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions#post844555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, in the W20 book. is there any art on Zhyzhak? im trying to find the She-Wolf of the Wyrm but i can seem to find her</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. But she has plenty of art in other books that can be found online and she's on the cover 2E Book of the Wyrm. In fact my favorite art piece of her came out in W20 Book of the Wyrm:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/wolf_1-copy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However I would shy away from using her in your games as she is the most power BSD in the game and one of, if not the most powerful living Garou in the setting. She's not the kind of foe the typical pack can handle. In fact I think she's only stat'ed in the final WtA book, <i>Apocalypse</i> and her stats are insane. In Homid she's Strength 7 and has been shown in art and fiction as able to kill Garou in Cinos with her bare hands as Homid.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why she's prophesized to kill the Last Gaian King during the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:38:42-08:00","id":844821,"title":"","content":"Not just prophesied, she DID kill Albrecht, who then used the Silver Fang gift of getting better from death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:49:49-08:00","id":844823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions?p=844821#post844821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just prophesied, she DID kill Albrecht, who then used the Silver Fang gift of getting better from death.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>one</i> version of the Apocalypse. In another she was potentially killed by the Perfect Metis, who had become the Avatar of the Balance Wyrm, the Wyrm as it was meant to be, before she ever got a chance at Albrecht.<br /> <br /> The Time of Judgement books and novels aren't canon because the books present multiple version on what the End is and how came to pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:31:31-08:00","id":844946,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/wolf_1-copy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Is it me or does the fact that the bottom half of Zhyzhak's face is in shadow make it look like she has a black beard? The first time I saw this picture, I was like &quot;That <i>can't</i> be Zhyzhak! This dude has a full-on beard! Wait, she has boobs. Who knew Zhyzhak was a bearded lady circus refugee with man-boobs, a nose that looks like a beak, and a six-pack abdomen?&quot;<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I didn't find this picture of Zhyzhak all that impressive. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Truth be told, the best picture of Zhyzhak I've seen is her on the cover of Book of the Wyrm, 2nd Edition. <i>Waaaaaay </i>better than the above picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 03-10-2016, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T23:34:12-08:00","id":844947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions?p=844946#post844946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/wolf_1-copy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Is it me or does the fact that the bottom half of Zhyzhak's face is in shadow make it look like she has a black beard? The first time I saw this picture, I was like &amp;quot;That <i>can't</i> be Zhyzhak! This dude has a full-on beard! Wait, she has boobs. Who knew Zhyzhak was a bearded lady circus refugee with man-boobs and a six-pack?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Some times the wyrm mutations work in mysterious ways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.j