pse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions?p=845105#post845105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game about shapeshifters has one shapeshifting in the picture. Her face is changing to match her hands, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I always saw that picture as her either in or transforming to Glabro form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:37:52-08:00","id":845598,"title":"","content":"I was wondering, if she is wearing a necklace made of teeth, or if it is her jaw, visible through the shadow that covers her lower face.<br /> The latter would indicate Glabro, the former could also be homid form or partial transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:23:25-08:00","id":845703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions?p=845324#post845324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>The word shemale is not appropriate here. Please do not use it. Thanks.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>sorry english it's not my native language edit like you want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:11:41-08:00","id":846070,"title":"","content":"When I start a Werewolf chronicle I generally start with a single theme and branch outward. For example: Suffer the Children<br /> Chapter one: A character's kinfolk sibling was kidnapped the pack intercepts the kidnapper but finds a map in the car with directions to a warehouse. A careful investigation reveals that it is the site of a auction of children. <br /> This particular story centered around the concept of corrupting children and the cycle of abuse. <br /> The villain in this case could be any number of things. I used a Nephandi mage. I could have used the 7th Generation or Pentex or even a bane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:11:17-07:00","id":847376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/844555-got-w20-any-advices-and-couple-o-questions#post844555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i recently got W20 and i gotta say, i loved the book.<br /> i used to play years ago with my original group/pack back in highschool and the book bought a lot of memories back.<br /> <br /> i been dming Mage for a long time now, love HtR and DtF. But dunno why, i find it a bit tricky to get a gasp on the mythos of Werewolf. i think its a huge game and universe but its hard for me to come up with ideas for games. to give it the epic/tragic style.. any advices on adventures, books or stories i should read from the Werewolf the apocalypse mythos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone already mentioned Rite of Passage, that's a great starting point, although it sounds like you're at least familiar with the basics of the game.<br /> <br /> When Will You Rage has been out a while now and is pretty easy to find on eBay or at used book stores, that has a lot of good stories that detail the themes and mythology of Werewolf. The newer version, Rites of Renown, is even better.<br /> <br /> I also really like the Apocalypse novel that ended the original series. It puts a lot of the big epic details front-and-center. If you can find the tribe novel series, even better, as that leads straight into Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The Revised Storytellers Handbook is also on DriveThruRPG right now for a reasonable price if you're ok with just the PDF. This will give you a lot of details on the overarching themes of the whole series.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:17:44-07:00","id":847379,"title":"","content":"Players Guide to Garou is another book good to get. It includes pretty much every details on garou. Only thing it doesn't, auspices, are handled by the book of Auspices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}